; pcrec VM program listing (DD-8; docs/design/engine_m4.md S10)
;
; Produced BY the emitter's own walk, not by a second walk over the
; AST: every line below was written by the same call that wrote the
; corresponding C. S10's one constraint -- "the dump must be derived
; from the same structure the emitter walks, never a parallel
; description" -- is therefore structural here, not a discipline.
;
; pattern      (?<=a|bc)x
; engine       vm (forced by: (?<=...) at pattern offset 0)
; prefilter    NO (--engine=vm) -- the VM scans from search_from itself (R21 E-6)
; rungs        none -- see the RUNGS section below for which quantifier took which
; strategies   none -- see the STRATEGIES section below for which quantifier took which
; possessify   0 of 0 source quantifiers possessified (eng_brep_design.md S2)
; caps         RX_NCAPS 1 (0 capturing groups in the pattern text)
; step budget  500000000 backtrack resumptions
; capacities   5 resume frames, 3 trail entries (exact: no subject ceiling)
; program      11 labels, 42 events
; resume pts   2
; max replicas 0 (limit 64, checked before emission)

SLOTS (the slot_values array, engine_m4.md S2.4)
  slot         holds                  note
   0,1         $0 whole match         written by the ENTRY, not the VM (S3.4)
  (no empty-iteration guard slots: no nullable unbounded quantifier on the frames rung)
  (no span-loop low-water slots: no cursor rung in this program)
  2            lookaround cut mark    resume-stack depth at the assertion's entry -- the atomic and negative forms commit ([M6.6.2])
  3            lookaround cursor      the entry position the assertion restores: a lookaround keeps the VERDICT and discards the POSITION

RUNGS (engine_m4.md S2.5; D46's per-quantifier stamp)
  (none: no quantifier in this program consulted the rung ladder at all)

STRATEGIES (eng_brep_design.md S2; D47.3's per-quantifier stamp)
  (none: this program has no quantifier to possessify)

PRUNING (k23_design.md; D51's per-quantifier stamp)
  ceiling: the subject end -- either no prefilter, or the prefilter's window END is not a bound on this match's end: the pattern carries an ATOMIC GROUP (atomic_groups_design.md 4.4 H3) or a LOOKAROUND (lookaround_design.md 5.6), or the prefilter was built from the COUNT-COLLAPSED superset (prefilter_count_independence.md 2 H3, K39/[OPT-4]) -- the `; prefilter` line above says which
  bound sites emitted: 0
  runtime-term length retreats: 0
  (none: this program has no quantifier to bound)

PROGRAM
  L0      ; positive lookbehind (atomic): record the resume-stack depth to cut back to, and the cursor to come back to (which is also what the END-CHECK compares against)
         set     slot_values[2] <- scan_position ; lookaround cut mark (resume-stack depth at the assertion's entry)
         set     slot_values[3] <- scan_position ; lookaround: the cursor to restore -- the assertion consumes nothing
         -> L4
  L4      ; lookbehind branch 1 of 2, fixed width 1: step back and run the branch FORWARD
         assert  lookbehind: fewer than 1 characters precede the cursor, so try the next branch -> L7
         PUSH    resume L7                    ; lookbehind: the NEXT-BRANCH continuation -- this branch's body failing retreats into the branch written after it
         ; work charge: the back-step, charged as the compile-time width rather than the runtime cost so the accounting does not depend on the encoding backend
         ; lookbehind: the ENCODING SEAM's back-step, 1 character
         ; lookbehind: the back-step ran off the start of the subject -- dead under the byte backend, where the guard above is exact
         -> L5
  L5
         consume 'a'                          -> L6
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L6      ; lookbehind END-CHECK: the branch must finish exactly where the assertion started -- the only runtime evidence that the width analysis and this emission agree
         ; lookbehind end-check FAILED -- this branch declines
         -> L3
  L7      ; lookbehind branch 2 of 2, fixed width 2: step back and run the branch FORWARD (the LAST branch: no retry frame)
         ; lookbehind: fewer than 2 characters precede the cursor, and this is the last branch -- the assertion fails here
         ; work charge: the back-step, charged as the compile-time width rather than the runtime cost so the accounting does not depend on the encoding backend
         ; lookbehind: the ENCODING SEAM's back-step, 2 characters
         ; lookbehind: the back-step ran off the start of the subject -- dead under the byte backend, where the guard above is exact
         -> L8
  L8
         consume 'b'                          -> L10
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L10
         consume 'c'                          -> L9
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L9      ; lookbehind END-CHECK: the branch must finish exactly where the assertion started -- the only runtime evidence that the width analysis and this emission agree
         ; lookbehind end-check FAILED -- this branch declines
         -> L3
  L3      ; positive lookaround: the body's FIRST success -- cut, restore the cursor, and never reconsider
         ; work charge: frames discarded by this cut
         CUT     frames <- slot_values[2]     ; cut: the assertion is committed; every choice point the body created is discarded, dead or not
         ; lookaround: the position is DISCARDED -- the cursor goes back to the assertion's entry
         -> L2
  L2
         consume 'x'                          -> L1
         -> fail (backtrack)
  L1      ; the pattern is complete
         -> accept
  accept   ; return scan_position - ctx->pos; the capture slots at this instant ARE the answer (S3.1)
  fail     ; the ONLY backtracker and the only indirect jump; one step charged here (S4.2)

CHOICE POINTS (preference order: the frame pushed at a site resumes the LESS preferred alternative)
  at L4      resume L7      lookbehind: the NEXT-BRANCH continuation -- this branch's body failing retreats into the branch written after it

DFA ISLANDS (0)
  (none: no flat alternation in this program has a finite literal language, so src/gen/emit_vm.c's alternation island declined every one -- docs/spec/tuning.md S2.20)

CALLOUT SITES (0)
  (none: module 'callouts' has no producer, so no pattern can reach a call site -- engine_m4.md S9.1)
